<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>kvm-it: third-party licences</title>
<style>
body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.4; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }
li { margin: 0.1rem 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>kvm-it is MIT-licensed. The desktop app (<code>kvmit</code>, <code>kvmit-gui</code>) is built from the open-source Rust
crates below, at the exact versions pinned in <code>desktop/Cargo.lock</code>. Each licence text is followed by the crates it
covers. Generated by cargo-about from the lockfile; the adapter firmware and iPXE are covered in
<code>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<h2>Licence texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}<li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
